<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tudhaliya IV</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tudhaliya IV was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> in the thirteenth century BCE, one of its last significant rulers. His reign saw extensive religious reorganisation and building, but also mounting pressures on the empire. The Hittite Empire profile lists succession conflicts after his death among the factors, along with drought, famine and the fragmentation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> network, that contributed to the empire's collapse.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tudhaliya-iv.jpg" alt="Tudhaliya IV" width="289" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:China_Crisis · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yazilikaya.TudhaliyaIV.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
